        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal African Rifles, Royal Navy, British Army\n- Products: Vickers machine gun\n- Companies: Vickers Limited\n- Ships: HMS Marlin\n- Events: August 1914 theft\n\nFacts:\n- In August 1914, a consignment of Vickers machine guns was stolen from the Royal Navy ship HMS Marlin.\n- The Vickers machine gun, also called the Vickers gun, primarily refers to a water-cooled .303 British (7.7 mm) machine gun.\n- Vickers Limited produced the Vickers machine gun originally for the British Army.",
